# Test: Prefix maximum enforcement tears down session (RFC 4486)
# AC-3: Peer sends prefixes exceeding family maximum (teardown=true) ->
#        NOTIFICATION Cease/MaxPrefixes sent, session torn down.
# AC-10: From spec-prefix-limit -- enforcement wiring test.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC4486-4-1 positive -- the daemon decides to terminate the peering because
# the received prefix count exceeds the configured upper bound, and the bytes below are the
# Cease NOTIFICATION section 4 requires: error code 06, subcode 01 ("Maximum Number of Prefixes
# Reached"), plus the optional Figure 1 Data field. The unit tags in
# internal/component/bgp/reactor/session_prefix_test.go prove the decision; this proves the
# running daemon puts that subcode on the wire to a real peer.

# ze-peer: sends 3 routes (exceeds maximum=2)
# Ze sends NOTIFICATION Cease/MaxPrefixes before EOR because it tears down.
# NOTIFICATION: code=6 (Cease), subcode=1 (MaxPrefixes),
# data=AFI(0001)+SAFI(01)+upper bound(00000002), the configured maximum per RFC 4486
# Section 4 Figure 1. The count that crossed it is 3 and never reaches the wire.
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=15s
option=asn:value=65001
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.0.0/24:next-hop=10.0.0.1
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.1.0/24:next-hop=10.0.0.1
option=update:value=send-route:prefix=10.0.2.0/24:next-hop=10.0.0.1
# Expect NOTIFICATION Cease/MaxPrefixes (type 3) instead of EOR
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF001C03060100010100000002
EOF_PEER

# ze bgp configuration: prefix maximum=2 for ipv4/unicast
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 10.0.0.1
			family {
				ipv4/unicast {
					prefix {
						maximum 2
					}
				}
			}
		}

	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=10s
# Verify enforcement happened via ze's stderr log
expect=stderr:contains=prefix count exceeded maximum
expect=stderr:contains=teardown
